cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use novelty-probe, please cite it as below."
title: "Novelty-probe: a logged, AI-assisted workflow for probing the literature around a research idea"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yuan"
    given-names: "Quan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3011-3739"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-11-03
repository-code: "https://github.com/PadSama/novelty-probe-demo"
abstract: >-
  An installable command-line workflow (novelty-probe) that breaks a research
  idea into facets, builds Boolean queries, searches OpenAlex and Semantic
  Scholar, merges and deduplicates the results with traceable rules, writes RIS,
  a run manifest and a PRISMA-S style search report, maps the top candidates to
  each facet of the idea, and verifies DOIs against Crossref. Every step is
  logged. It collects evidence and does not judge novelty.
keywords:
  - literature search
  - research workflow
  - OpenAlex
  - Semantic Scholar
  - Crossref
  - science of science
license: MIT
